      "answer": "Here is what *Poison* does in Gloomhaven (2nd Edition), per the rulebook:\n\n> **Poison:** All attacks targeting the figure gain \"+1 [attack modifier draw].\" Poison is removed when the figure is healed but, unlike wound, poison prevents the heal from increasing the figure's current hit point value.\n\n**In summary:**\n- Any attack against a *Poisoned* figure gets **+1** to its attack modifier draws.\n- *Poison* is removed when the figure receives a *Heal* — but that heal **does not restore any HP**. The condition is cleansed, but the healing value is wasted.\n\n*(Source: Gloomhaven 2nd Edition Rulebook, Negative Conditions section)*",
