      "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
      "agentRuntime": "langgraph",
      "ok": true,
      "answer": "Here's how **long rests** work in Frosthaven:\n\n---\n\n**Declaring a Long Rest**\nDuring the **Card Selection** step, instead of selecting two cards to play, a character with at least two cards in their *discard pile* may declare a long rest. Their entire turn for the round is the long rest, and it is performed on **initiative 99**.\n\n**Long Rest Steps (in order):**\n\n1. **Lose one card of their choice** from their discard pile and return the remaining cards to their hand. *(Mandatory)*\n2. **Perform \"*Heal* 2, self.\"** *(Optional)*\n3. **Recover all spent *items*.** Items can even be used during the same turn they are recovered. *(Optional)*\n\n---\n\n**Key Points:**\n- You must have **at least two cards** in your discard pile to rest (either short or long).\n- Resting **always results in losing one card** — but with a long rest, you get to *choose* which card you lose.\n- Unlike a short rest (which happens during the End of Round step), a long rest replaces your normal turn entirely.\n\n*Source: Frosthaven Rulebook, passages 72 & 125*",
