      "ok": true,
      "answer": "Here is the *Poison* condition as defined in the **Gloomhaven (2nd Edition)** rulebook and FAQ:\n\n---\n\n### *Poison* — Gloomhaven (2nd Edition)\n\n**Core rule:**\n\n> **Poison:** All attacks targeting the figure gain \"+1 ★\". Poison is removed when the figure is healed but, unlike wound, poison prevents the heal from increasing the figure's current hit point value.\n\n*(Rulebook, passage 114)*\n\n**Interaction with *Heal*:**\n\n> A single heal can remove both wound and poison from a figure. However, if poison is present, the hit point increase is prevented.\n\n*(Rulebook, passage 118)*\n\n---\n\n### Key FAQ Clarifications *(FAQ, passages 29 & 71)*\n\n- **Non-stackable:** *Poison* cannot stack. If multiple sources attempt to apply it in one attack, only one instance applies — a single *Safeguard* still fully prevents it.\n- **Giving *Poison* to allies:** Some abilities allow a character to give *Poison* to an ally. If the ally prevents the condition (e.g., via *Safeguard*), the character still fulfills any requirement tied to applying it.\n- **Immunity doesn't block the give:** You can give *Poison* to an ally who is immune to it; the condition simply has no effect on them.\n- **Objectives cannot receive *Poison*** or any other condition.\n- **No Line of Sight required** to give *Poison* to an ally, since \"give\" is not a targeted ability — though range still cannot be counted through walls.",
